## Commit Message Format

### Commit Message Structure

When committing changes, use this format:

```
<type>: <short summary>

PROBLEM:
- Describe the issue or problem being solved
- List specific symptoms or user complaints
- Include error messages or unexpected behaviors

SOLUTION:
- Explain the approach taken to fix the problem
- List key changes made (components, patterns)
- Reference any design patterns or best practices applied
- Include technical details

BENEFITS:
- List improvements (UX, performance, maintainability)
- Note any code reuse or component extraction
- Mention consistency improvements

FILES CHANGED:
- List all modified files with brief description
- Note new files created
- Mention refactored files
```

### Commit Types

- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `refactor`: Code refactoring without changing functionality
- `test`: Adding or updating tests
- `docs`: Documentation changes
- `chore`: Maintenance tasks, dependencies
- `perf`: Performance improvements

### Example Commit Message

```
feat: Add comprehensive testing infrastructure

PROBLEM:
- No automated testing framework in place
- Manual testing required for all changes
- No coverage reporting
- Difficult to catch regressions

SOLUTION:
- Set up pytest with comprehensive configuration
- Created shared fixtures in conftest.py
- Added unit tests for capital, risk, position sizing
- Added integration tests for end-to-end flow
- Integrated with GitHub Actions for CI/CD
- Added coverage reporting with 70% minimum threshold

BENEFITS:
- Automated testing catches bugs early
- Coverage reporting ensures code quality
- CI/CD integration provides continuous testing
- Shared fixtures reduce test code duplication

FILES CHANGED:
- pytest.ini (new) - Pytest configuration
- tests/conftest.py (new) - Shared fixtures
- tests/unit/test_capital_manager.py (new) - Unit tests
- tests/integration/test_end_to_end_flow.py (new) - Integration tests
- .github/workflows/tests.yml (new) - CI/CD workflow
- Makefile (new) - Test commands
- tests/README.md (new) - Test documentation
```

